\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Autoregressive continuation law}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{language-model}

\p{The \newvocab{autoregressive continuation law} induced by
#{\pi_\theta} assigns a continuation #{x_{t+1:T}} to a prefix #{x_{1:t}} the
conditional probability
##{
\pi_\theta(x_{t+1:T}\mid x_{1:t})
=\prod_{s=t+1}^{T}\pi_\theta(x_s\mid x_{<s}).
}
The product uses the newly generated tokens when forming each later prefix.}

\p{This factorization is the causal product used by decoder-only sequence
modelling in \citet{sec. 3}{phuong2022formal}. It defines probabilities of
fixed finite continuations. A sampling rule and a termination rule are still
needed to obtain a random variable-length generation procedure.}
